atlas evidence-appliance-release-manifest

architecture appliance-release-manifest
  canonical_name ApplianceReleaseManifest
  owns BuildTreeArtifactInventory
  publishes ApplianceCompatibilityManifest
  publishes ManifestReleaseNotes
  family evidence
  domain Evidence / Build artifact inventory
  layer packaging
  semantic_question Which current build-tree operators, native libraries and model representation aliases are described by the appliance compatibility manifest and its release notes?
  purpose Restore the legacy appliance manifest and notes contract through one Bun compiler, without interpreting archived Python or confusing a build-tree inventory with a seal, signature or running-process attestation.
  maturity implemented
  source_path scripts/appliance-manifest.mjs
  source_path scripts/gen_manifest.py.archive
  source_path scripts/release_notes_from_manifest.py.archive
  source_path Makefile
  source_path Aurekai/Makefile
  witness scripts/tests/appliance_manifest.test.mjs proves archived executable filtering, stable binary and library hashes, model and SAE aliases, dotted FPQx identities, optional fallback, exact release-note formatting, actual root Make targets in an isolated fixture without Python, and previous-report preservation on malformed input
  internal_calculus sorted build-tree artifacts -> streaming SHA-256 with file identity checks -> bonfyre.deploy.v1 inventory -> manifest-derived Markdown release notes
  internal_calculus legacy and Aurekai model aliases -> one family entry; SAE aliases -> one dictionary entry; FPQx aliases -> full dotted-stem entry
  invariant only executable bonfyre or bonfyre-prefixed regular files directly under a command directory enter the operator inventory; artifacts are hashed and never executed
  invariant operator and library hashing rejects file identity or metadata changes during the read, using bounded streaming buffers rather than whole-binary allocations
  invariant generated runtime FFI drift and runnable-capability states remain unknown without evidence; enumeration cannot establish either
  invariant the historical optional default-model paths remain compatibility hints with explicit not_observed presence when no model descriptor exists
  invariant release notes preserve public model aliases and distinct legacy paths; malformed structures and multiline scalar labels refuse before replacing an existing report
  invariant a completed output is renamed from a same-directory temporary file; partial generator failures do not replace the existing output
  invariant root manifest produces both root and dist compatibility paths; release-notes depends on the same manifest and consumes its dist copy
  forbidden_inference a manifest, SHA-256 inventory or generated release notes -> correct binaries, FFI zero drift, runnable capabilities, resident fallback weights, signed provenance, authorized deployment or the bytes actually running
  known_gap compatibility revision is a short Git label, not a complete reproducible source and toolchain closure; the signature field remains explicitly unsigned
  known_gap the fixture witnesses packaging metadata only; the complete appliance build, runtime pack and installation are not executed by these tests
  interacts running-system-attestation

interaction appliance-inventory-distinct-from-runtime-attestation
  source appliance-release-manifest
  destination running-system-attestation
  relation build_tree_inventory_is_distinct_from_deployed_and_running_bytes
  preserves artifact names and content digests as observations of a named build tree
  drops any inference that a build-tree artifact has been sealed, installed, authorized or started
  authority deployment and running-process byte attestation remain owned by the existing seal, deploy and runtime attestation operations
  forbidden_inference generated release metadata -> sealed equals deployed equals running
  witness scripts/tests/appliance_manifest.test.mjs
  binding scripts/appliance-manifest.mjs
  binding scripts/release_attest.mjs
